  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">A Sense of Brutality (2020), published by Amherst College Press, has been cited 3 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 1,654 times and is used in teaching.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">A Sense of Brutality by Carlos Sánchez was published by Amherst College Press in 2020. Conceptually, the work connects to Police brutality, Sense (electronics), Psychology, Criminology and Engineering. The book was recognised: ACLS Open Access Book Prize & Arcadia Open Access Publishing Award finalist (2026) — Political Science.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 3 citations. Citations peaked in 2021 with 1 citing works. Notable citing venues include Ethical Theory and Moral Practice and Journal of the Academy. The citing works include 2 journal articles and 1 book chapter. They come from 3 countries, led by Chile, the Netherlands and the United States.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In teaching, it is discussed in 1 recorded lecture. It has been downloaded 1,654 times via OAPEN. It is recorded in 1 library collection. Its subject matter aligns with Peace, Justice and strong institutions among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>",
